ada  (Spanish: Virreinato del Nuevo Reino de Granada [birejˈnato ðel ˈnweβo ˈrejno ðe ɣɾaˈnaða]), also called Viceroyalty of New Granada (Virreinato de la Nueva Granada) or Viceroyalty of Santa Fe, was the name given on 27 May 1717 to the jurisdiction of the Spanish Empire in northern South America, corresponding to modern Colombia, Ecuador, Panama and Venezuela. \nCreated in 1717 by King Felipe V, as part of a new territorial control policy, it was suspended in 1723 for financial problems. It was restored in 1739 until the independence movement suspended it again in 1810. The territory corresponding to Panama was incorporated in 1739."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q8965","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q2841","value_label":"Bogotá","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Bogotá"},{"qid":"Q8965","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q2077264","value_label":"New Kingdom of Granada","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1365","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"New Kingdom of Granada"},{"qid":"Q8965","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q199821","value_label":"Gran Colombia","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Gran Colombia"}],"people":{},"media":{},"names":["Colonial Colombia","Neu-Granada","New Granada","Nouvelle-Grenade","Nova Granada","Nueva Granada","Onderkoninkrijk Nieuw-Granada","Spanish Colombia","Spanish Ecuador","Spanish Venezuela","Terra Ferma","Terra Firma","Terre Ferme","Vice-Reino de Nova Granada","Vicereame della Nuova Granada","Viceroyalty of New Granada","Virreinato de Nueva Granada","Virreinato de Nueva Granada, Virreinato de Santafé o","Virreinato de Santa Fé","Virreinato de Santafé","Virreinato de la Nueva Granada","Virreinato del Nuevo Reino de Granada","Vizekönigreich Neugranada","Wicekrólestwo Nowej Granady","Yeni Granada Kral Vekilliği","vice-royauté de Nouvelle-Grenade","Новая Гранада","النيابة الملكية على غرناطة الجديدة","نایب‌الملک‌نشین گرانادای جدید","ヌエ